  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two trolleys, X and Y, with masses of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\text{ kg}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\\text{ kg}\"></span> respectively, are initially at rest on a frictionless horizontal surface with a compressed spring held between them.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The system is released. What is the value of the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\text{kinetic energy of trolley X}}{\\text{kinetic energy of trolley Y}}\"></span> at the instant the trolleys lose contact with the spring?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0.16</li><li data-label=\"B\">0.40</li><li data-label=\"C\">1.0</li><li data-label=\"D\">2.5</li></ol>"
  },
